---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { buildAmazonProductUrl } from "@/config/affiliate";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Best Coconut Milk for Keto: Full-Fat & Low-Carb Picks (2026)"
  description="Coconut milk is a keto staple for Thai curries. We rank the best full-fat, additive-free coconut milk brands for flavor, fat content, and carb count."
  canonical="https://thaiketo.com/roundups/best-coconut-milk-keto"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
    <header class="mb-10 text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 mb-4">
        <span class="badge badge-primary text-xs">Product Roundup</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-neutral-500">August 12, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-display font-semibold text-primary leading-tight mb-4">
        Best Coconut Milk for Keto: Full-Fat & Low-Carb Picks
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Coconut milk is a keto staple for Thai curries. We rank the best full-fat, additive-free coconut milk brands.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-thai">
      <h2>Why Coconut Milk Quality Matters on Keto</h2>
      <p>Coconut milk is the backbone of Thai curries and a keto superfood — it's rich in medium-chain triglycerides (MCTs), low in carbs, and adds incredible creaminess to dishes. But not all coconut milk is created equal. Many brands add thickeners like guar gum, emulsifiers, and even sugar. Others are watered down, reducing the fat content that makes coconut milk so valuable on keto.</p>
      <p>We tested six popular coconut milk brands to find the best options for keto Thai cooking. Our criteria: fat content, carb count, ingredient purity, and flavor.</p>

      <h2>What to Look for in Keto Coconut Milk</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Full-fat only:</strong> Light coconut milk has fewer fats and proportionally more carbs. Always choose full-fat.</li>
        <li><strong>Minimal ingredients:</strong> The best coconut milk contains just coconut and water. Guar gum is acceptable but unnecessary.</li>
        <li><strong>No added sugar:</strong> Some brands add sugar. Always check the label.</li>
        <li><strong>BPA-free cans:</strong> Coconut milk is acidic and can leach BPA from can linings. Look for BPA-free packaging.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold text-primary mb-6">Product Comparison</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-primary-50 text-left">
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-primary">Product</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-primary">Rating</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-primary">Price</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-primary">Buy</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200">
              <td class="p-3"><div class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Aroy-D 100% Coconut Milk</div><div class="text-xs text-neutral-500 mt-1">Pure coconut milk with no additives. Rich, creamy, and the gold standard for Thai cooking...</div></td>
              <td class="p-3"><div class="flex items-center gap-1"><span class="text-accent font-semibold">4.8</span><span class="text-accent">★</span></div></td>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-neutral-700">$3.99</td>
              <td class="p-3"><a href={buildAmazonProductUrl("B00ITC3IK0")} target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="btn btn-amazon btn-sm text-xs">View on Amazon</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200">
              <td class="p-3"><div class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Chaokoh Coconut Milk</div><div class="text-xs text-neutral-500 mt-1">Another Thai brand with excellent flavor. Slightly sweeter than Aroy-D, great for Panang curry...</div></td>
              <td class="p-3"><div class="flex items-center gap-1"><span class="text-accent font-semibold">4.6</span><span class="text-accent">★</span></div></td>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-neutral-700">$3.49</td>
              <td class="p-3"><a href={buildAmazonProductUrl("B00852ZN2U")} target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="btn btn-amazon btn-sm text-xs">View on Amazon</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200">
              <td class="p-3"><div class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Native Forest Organic Coconut Milk</div><div class="text-xs text-neutral-500 mt-1">USDA organic, BPA-free can. Clean flavor, no additives. Slightly less rich than Thai brands...</div></td>
              <td class="p-3"><div class="flex items-center gap-1"><span class="text-accent font-semibold">4.4</span><span class="text-accent">★</span></div></td>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-neutral-700">$4.49</td>
              <td class="p-3"><a href={buildAmazonProductUrl("B001HTJ2BQ")} target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="btn btn-amazon btn-sm text-xs">View on Amazon</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200">
              <td class="p-3"><div class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Thai Kitchen Organic Coconut Milk</div><div class="text-xs text-neutral-500 mt-1">Widely available in US grocery stores. Contains guar gum. Decent but not the best for authentic Thai flavor...</div></td>
              <td class="p-3"><div class="flex items-center gap-1"><span class="text-accent font-semibold">3.8</span><span class="text-accent">★</span></div></td>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-neutral-700">$3.29</td>
              <td class="p-3"><a href={buildAmazonProductUrl("B000LKZ924")} target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="btn btn-amazon btn-sm text-xs">View on Amazon</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-neutral-200">
              <td class="p-3"><div class="font-medium text-neutral-900">365 by Whole Foods Organic Coconut Milk</div><div class="text-xs text-neutral-500 mt-1">Good value organic option. Contains guar gum. Solid everyday choice...</div></td>
              <td class="p-3"><div class="flex items-center gap-1"><span class="text-accent font-semibold">4.1</span><span class="text-accent">★</span></div></td>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium text-neutral-700">$2.99</td>
              <td class="p-3"><a href={buildAmazonProductUrl("B07FXXK3M2")} target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" class="btn btn-amazon btn-sm text-xs">View on Amazon</a></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="prose-thai mt-8">
      <h2>Our Top Pick: Aroy-D</h2>
      <p>Aroy-D is the gold standard for Thai coconut milk. It contains 100% coconut milk with no additives — no guar gum, no emulsifiers, no preservatives. The fat content is consistently high (17-19g per 1/2 cup), and the flavor is clean, rich, and authentic. This is what Thai restaurants use.</p>

      <h2>Runner-Up: Chaokoh</h2>
      <p>Chaokoh is another excellent Thai brand with a slightly sweeter, more aromatic profile. It's our top pick for Panang and Massaman curries where a touch of natural sweetness is desirable. The fat content is comparable to Aroy-D.</p>

      <h2>Best Organic: Native Forest</h2>
      <p>If organic certification and BPA-free packaging are important to you, Native Forest is the best choice. The flavor is slightly less rich than the Thai brands, but it's still very good. The BPA-free can is a nice bonus for a product as acidic as coconut milk.</p>

      <h2>Avoid: Thai Kitchen</h2>
      <p>Thai Kitchen is the most widely available brand in US supermarkets, but it's also the most disappointing. It contains guar gum, which gives it a slightly slimy texture, and the coconut flavor is noticeably weaker than the Thai brands. It works in a pinch, but Aroy-D or Chaokoh will give you much better results.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-8 text-center">
      As an Amazon Associate, ThaiKeto earns from qualifying purchases.
    </p>
  </article>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "Best Coconut Milk for Keto: Full-Fat & Low-Carb Picks",
    "description": "Coconut milk is a keto staple for Thai curries. We rank the best full-fat, additive-free coconut milk brands.",
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "ThaiKeto Team" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "ThaiKeto" },
    "datePublished": "2026-08-12",
    "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://thaiketo.com/roundups/best-coconut-milk-keto" }
  })} />
</BaseLayout>
